Package: postgresql-@PG@-pg-sift
Architecture: any
Depends: postgresql-@PG@, ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: Fast analytics for PostgreSQL: keep your queries, just add an index. Plus BM25 full-text search
 pg_sift answers counts, sums, distinct counts, group-bys and top-N from
 compressed columns, with the queries you already have: a sift_col index on a
 table, or the sift_table table access method, is picked by the planner through
 the SiftAgg aggregate scan, and a query the planner cannot prove equal keeps
 PostgreSQL's own plan.
 .
 It also adds BM25 full-text search: a sift index answers boolean, phrase,
 prefix, wildcard, regex and fuzzy queries with exact ranking, through its own
 query syntax.
 .
 One CREATE EXTENSION, no shared_preload_libraries. For PostgreSQL 17, 18 and
 19.
